  "final_message": "I am listing the workspace directory to inspect the project layout and locate the `orders-service` files.\nI have started running `npm test` to verify the initial state of the test suite.\nI am searching for all references to `channel` within the `orders-service` codebase.\nI am searching for references to `channel` across the other repositories to understand how `OrderPlaced` and `channel` are used elsewhere.\nI am checking if `billing-service` uses `channel`.\nI am checking `web-storefront` for references to `channel`.\nI am checking how `web-storefront` calls the orders service.\nI am running the unit tests in `analytics-ingest` to observe its expectations.\nI am checking the recent git commit history to see recent context.\nI am checking `git status` to see if there are any modified or untracked files.\nI am inspecting the commit details.\nI am checking the root workspace directory for any hidden files or configuration.\nI am checking for any git branches or tags.\nI am checking the `.git` directory.\nI am checking cross-repository references to `analytics-ingest`.\nI am checking the environment setup to see if there is any other context.\nI am running `npm run arch` in `orders-service` to check the dependency architecture rules.\nI am checking for any architecture documentation files.\nThe `channel` field cannot be dropped from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event and order model because the premise that nothing reads the field is incorrect.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed\n\nThe downstream service **`analytics-ingest`** (team Data) actively depends on `channel` in the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event:\n\n1. **Strict Contract Validation**:\n   - In [`decodeOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L25-L46), `analytics-ingest` validates that `channel` is present and matches one of `\"web\" | \"store\" | \"marketplace\"`.\n   - If `channel` is omitted, it throws a [`ContractViolationError`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/errors.ts#L14) and rejects the event (enforced by tests in [ingest.test.ts](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts#L88-L94)).\n2. **Data Lake Ingestion**:\n   - In [`ingestOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts#L12-L24), the field is written directly to the data lake table schema [`OrderRow`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/rows.ts#L5-L11).\n\nDropping `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/orders-service/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) and [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) in `orders-service` would break the contract with `analytics-ingest` and cause downstream ingestion to fail. \n\nBefore removing this field, the contract must first be coordinated with team Data to update `analytics-ingest`.\n",
